# =============================================================================
# DotNetNuke migration repository — root ignore rules
#
# This repository hosts a side-by-side ("strangler pattern") technology
# migration. The modern trees — backend/ (C# 12 / .NET 8 ASP.NET Core API) and
# frontend/ (Angular 19 SPA) — live ALONGSIDE the original VB.NET trees
# Library/ and Website/, which are read-only reference inputs: they must remain
# byte-identical and fully tracked, and the legacy solutions must stay
# buildable. Nothing here may change the git status of a single legacy file.
#
# Two properties of this repository shape the rules below. Anyone editing this
# file must preserve both, or tracked legacy sources start disappearing from
# `git status` on other developers' machines:
#
#   1. The legacy trees COMMIT their pre-built bin/ assemblies to source
#      control — 52 tracked .dll/.xml files across 8 bin/ directories. The
#      build-output rules are therefore followed by explicit directory
#      negations; see "Legacy committed binaries" below.
#
#   2. Several patterns in everyday use collide with real legacy directory
#      names — Library/Components/Packages/, Website/admin/Packages/ and
#      Website/Portals/_default/Logs/. Those patterns are ANCHORED to the new
#      trees with a leading slash instead of being applied repository-wide.
#      Never un-anchor them: git folds case when matching ignore patterns on
#      any clone where core.ignorecase is true (macOS and Windows), so a bare
#      `packages/` or `logs/` rule silently swallows those legacy sources even
#      though the casing differs.
#
# Verify any change to this file with:
#   git ls-files | git check-ignore --no-index --stdin
# It must print nothing. `--no-index` is required — without it git reports
# already-tracked files as "not ignored" and masks exactly this class of bug.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output — required exclusions
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Legacy committed binaries — DO NOT ignore
#
# These directories hold source-less, pre-built reference assemblies that are
# already under source control and that the legacy build links against
# directly. Dropping them would break DotNetNuke.sln and destroy the only copy
# of binaries that have no source anywhere in the checkout, for example:
#   Library/Components/DataAccessBlock/bin/Microsoft.ApplicationBlocks.Data.dll
#       — the SqlHelper implementation the entire legacy ADO.NET layer calls
#   Library/Controls/DotNetNuke.WebControls/bin/DotNetNuke.WebControls.dll
#   Library/Components/SharpZipLib/bin/SharpZipLib.dll
#       — both referenced by HintPath from Library/DotNetNuke.Library.vbproj
#   Website/bin/*.dll + *.xml  — 44 tracked files, the deployed legacy binaries
#
# Git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, so these
# negations re-include the DIRECTORIES themselves (`!Website/bin/`), not their
# contents (`!Website/bin/**`, which does NOT work). They must stay AFTER the
# `[Bb]in/` rule above — for ignore rules, the last matching pattern wins.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
!Website/bin/
!Library/**/bin/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .NET build, test and tooling artefacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*
msbuild.log
*.user
*.userosscache
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.dbmdl
*.log
.vs/
artifacts/
project.lock.json

# Test and coverage output (`dotnet test`, coverlet.collector).
# The `coverage*` globs use a single wildcard on purpose so they catch both
# coverlet's default file names (coverage.json, coverage.info) and its
# format-qualified ones (coverage.cobertura.xml, coverage.opencover.xml).
# No tracked file in this repository has a basename beginning "coverage".
TestResults/
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
*.trx
*.coverage
*.coverlet.json
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NuGet
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
.nuget/packages/

# The packages.config-era restore folder. ANCHORED to the backend solution on
# purpose — an un-anchored `packages/` rule matches the legacy VB source trees
# Library/Components/Packages/ (34 tracked files) and Website/admin/Packages/
# (7 tracked files) on any case-insensitive clone. backend/DnnMigration.sln
# restores via PackageReference into the global cache, so this folder should
# never appear at all; the rule exists only as a guard.
/backend/packages/*
!/backend/packages/build/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Entity Framework Core — intentionally NOTHING is ignored
#
# backend/src/DnnMigration.Infrastructure/Persistence/Migrations/ holds the
# baseline migration and MUST be committed. It is deliberately a no-op that
# only seeds __EFMigrationsHistory, because the legacy schema is immutable and
# depends on externally installed aspnet_* objects. Never ignore Migrations/.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / Angular
#
# NOTE: frontend/package-lock.json and frontend/karma.conf.js are
# gate-critical and must never be ignored — `npm ci` fails outright without a
# committed lockfile, and the headless-Chrome test run fails outright without
# the karma config. Do not add `package-lock.json` or `*-lock.json` here.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.angular/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
chrome-profiler-events*.json
speed-measure-plugin*.json

# Explicit anchors for the Angular workspace output (also covered by the
# repository-wide `dist/` and `coverage/` rules above).
/frontend/dist/
/frontend/coverage/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime log directories
#
# ANCHORED for the same reason as the NuGet rule: a bare `logs/` would match
# Website/Portals/_default/Logs/, which has tracked files.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/backend/logs/
/frontend/logs/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE and editor state
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS noise
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local environment overrides
#
# Real credentials never enter source control. Only the committed
# docker/.env.example template documents the required variables, and
# appsettings.json / appsettings.Development.json / appsettings.Production.json
# are tracked configuration — only *.local.json overlays are ignored.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.env
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
appsettings.*.local.json
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key

# Keep the credential-free template that docker-compose.yml documents.
!docker/.env.example
